    "title": "Camp Hope 2026 - Returning Families",
    "intro_text": "Camper Experiences\n\nThere are three unique camper experiences offered at Camp Hope depending on the grade level completed, depending on their grade level completed. They are:\n\n• Camper - Just finished 2nd grade through finished 7th grade\n\n• Senior Camper - Just finished 8th grade - This is a program tailored to provide a unique, fun, and challenging experience for this age group - a highlight for many past senior campers! It includes special events off campus and powerful talks and witnesses offering a vision for choosing to live for Christ as they enter their high school years. As a note, due to the offsite activities of this program campers are asked to bring some extra money. The details of which will be communicated to registered families in advance of camp.\n\n• C.L.A.S. Act - Catholic Love in Active Service - Just finished 9th grade - This is still a camper registration. This program offers several types of experiences. 1) Challenges on and off campus to learn to offer themselves in service to others. 2) The necessary training for being a counselor and support to activities at Camp Hope. A past highlight for 9th graders has been planning and a running a night activity for boys and girls at camp. 3) Talks and activities tailored to this group. They will be in their own cabin grouping with some great adults to lead, support and work along side them. Further details about this program including spending money and permission forms will be emailed to registered families in advance of camp.\n\nTo pay for Camp Hope by check, please select the \"Pay Later\" option. Checks should be made out to \"Camp Hope\", with the names of the campers in the memo line. Checks should be mailed to \"People of Hope, 1040 Plainfield Ave, Plainfield, NJ 07060\" and must be received by July 1.\n\nPlease read before you register\n\nSome cabins are full or nearly full, so registering does not guarantee a spot for your camper.\n\n• 3rd Grade Boys: No Availability\n\n• 3rd Grade Girls: Limited Availability\n\n• 5th Grade Girls: No Availability\n\n• 6th Grade Girls: No Availability\n\n• 7th Grade Girls: No Availability\n\nDo NOT register a camper for a cabin with no availability. Instead, please email camphope.poh@gmail.com with the name/grade/gender of your child and request to be put on a waitlist.",
    "success_text": "Thank you for registering for Camp Hope. You will receive an email with additional information.\n\nCamp forms and documents can be found on the Important Documents page (https://www.camphoperegistration.com/important-documents/).\n\nCompleted forms must be scanned or photographed and uploaded by July 1st using the Camp Hope Document Upload portal linked HERE (https://form.jotform.com/211527447357055). Please be aware of the Cancellation Policy (https://www.camphoperegistration.com/faqs/#cancellation).",
    "submit_label": "Register",
